#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb23c291-a2fb-5e57-bbc9-7b2c02d0a1ea" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Riccati Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e02fb666-75ba-5aa2-a3f4-f2eed84f478b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{x} - \\frac{1}{x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216436} {:answer/id #uuid "048e80d9-1ef6-5b08-afb9-376af0c12143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{x} + \\frac{2}{x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216437} {:answer/id #uuid "423229b3-99af-5437-8b2c-25093d497a66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{x} + \\frac{2}{x - C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216438} {:answer/id #uuid "67d9ab9f-6284-5350-bb22-a7234d9bee2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{x} - \\frac{1}{2x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216439} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9e8880-c902-5ca1-86d0-24166a394641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{x} + \\frac{1}{x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e02fb666-75ba-5aa2-a3f4-f2eed84f478b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{x} - \\frac{1}{x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216436} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4288d21-83df-55cd-94f8-7f2cea06b36c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df799e88-0866-5ce2-876c-d28588733f23" :question/math-academy-id "q-321225" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-2{e}^{x}y+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." :question/worked-solution "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-2{e}^{x}y+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=1,\\,b(x)=-2{e}^{x},\\,c(x)={e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{e}^{x}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+{e}^{x}=(z+{e}^{x})^{2}-2{e}^{x}(z+{e}^{x})+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & =({e}^{2x}+2{e}^{x}z+{z}^{2})-(2{e}^{2x}+2{e}^{x}z)+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & ={z}^{2}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′} & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-{e}^{x}$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{x+C} \\\\ y-{e}^{x} & =-\\frac{1}{x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{x+C}+{e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c5fc503-d0bb-54e3-8192-dbb30aef1d27" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a Riccati Differential Equation to a Bernoulli Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eb032ba-854c-572f-b02d-5d5a59039885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349653} {:answer/id #uuid "e78a88e7-3623-5181-90ba-2aee6d1dacae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9eb032ba-854c-572f-b02d-5d5a59039885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349653} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae6a07ab-7cd9-5202-aa98-6288674af8ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216519} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44f97dae-b00a-5efa-b871-3686cb439684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44f97dae-b00a-5efa-b871-3686cb439684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349655} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eb314e8-f9ab-57bb-8fd8-c1cb7aa4bc85" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216520} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea5ccfe0-b07b-566b-9318-1899942b3a79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea5ccfe0-b07b-566b-9318-1899942b3a79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349656} :answer-field/id #uuid "77a51392-d4ae-5111-beaa-2b5e75f329c0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23e786fd-45e8-5025-bad8-5c78c0494a27" :question/math-academy-id "q-332991" :question/problem "The function ${y}_{0}(x)=-x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{y}^{2}-(2x+1)y-(1+x+{x}^{2}).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=-x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-1$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z-x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-1.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-1=-(z-x)^{2}-(2x+1)(-x+z)-(1+x+{x}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-1 & =-({x}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2xz)-(-2{x}^{2}+2xz-x+z)-(1+x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ {z}^{′}-1 & =-{z}^{2}-z-1 \\\\ {z}^{′}+z & =-{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=1,\\,Q(x)=-1,\\,n=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c5fc503-d0bb-54e3-8192-dbb30aef1d27" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a Riccati Differential Equation to a Bernoulli Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20316b5e-87ee-58b6-9453-df38791ade65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20316b5e-87ee-58b6-9453-df38791ade65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349659} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc12e19a-1bed-54e0-9879-4e3b17d20c5a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94de50b2-d6b0-5dd7-8825-1aa2c9bc4b07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94de50b2-d6b0-5dd7-8825-1aa2c9bc4b07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349661} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c5c1ea3-35b6-518c-8e50-d3236963f495" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349660} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8e0cf2a-1d05-5ea6-8d76-f6519ae06de5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8e0cf2a-1d05-5ea6-8d76-f6519ae06de5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349663} :answer-field/id #uuid "96b328f5-a3b7-56ce-b6a0-9956feba25ec" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3dbcebde-af6e-556b-a609-8e3b250e9430" :question/math-academy-id "q-333616" :question/problem "The function ${y}_{0}(x)={x}^{2}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}-2x({x}^{2}+1)y+x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={x}^{2}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=2x$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{x}^{2}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+2x.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+2x=x(z+{x}^{2})^{2}-2x({x}^{2}+1)(z+{x}^{2})+x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+2x & =x(z+{x}^{2})^{2}-2x({x}^{2}+1)(z+{x}^{2})+x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2) \\\\ {z}^{′}+2x & =x{z}^{2}-2xz+2x \\\\ {z}^{′}+2xz & =x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=2x,\\,Q(x)=x,\\,n=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb23c291-a2fb-5e57-bbc9-7b2c02d0a1ea" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Riccati Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81538363-f3f8-5430-a0ee-e99fffd573b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349666} {:answer/id #uuid "479cf870-ce0d-5c84-837a-713e220be050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349667} {:answer/id #uuid "0b0d8718-4b2f-5b6a-9b1e-eee0f30f5489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349668} {:answer/id #uuid "f0cc9a0f-889f-5fbe-ad4f-6ce5717bbd9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349669} {:answer/id #uuid "144a4dcb-44b9-5d8c-ae73-8d1ba11faddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "479cf870-ce0d-5c84-837a-713e220be050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349667} :answer-field/id #uuid "736d0edf-2620-5ef7-a342-b4bde0a23520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "262f720c-cbdd-503c-9647-53ea02489b2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334117" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=3x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-12{x}^{2}y+18{x}^{3}+3\n$$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." :question/worked-solution "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-12{x}^{2}y+18{x}^{3}+3,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=2x,\\,b(x)=-12{x}^{2},\\,c(x)=18{x}^{3}+3.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=3x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=3$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+3x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+3.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+3=2x\\,(z+3x)^{2}-12{x}^{2}(z+3x)+18{x}^{3}+3.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+3 & =2x(9{x}^{2}+6xz+{z}^{2})-12{x}^{2}z-36{x}^{3}+18{x}^{3}+3 \\\\ {z}^{′}+3 & =2x{z}^{2}+3 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =2x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-3x$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y-3x & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}+3x \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb23c291-a2fb-5e57-bbc9-7b2c02d0a1ea" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Riccati Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1828e785-cc99-5b8c-947b-569b4f6b2064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6x+\\frac{2}{3x-C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349673} {:answer/id #uuid "56f788fc-a267-5197-9a25-a60283bfb398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6x-\\frac{1}{3x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349674} {:answer/id #uuid "e4279bab-25e7-5546-b407-1ea471c1756f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6x-\\frac{1}{x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349675} {:answer/id #uuid "1ed37381-8876-57d1-a9f5-4e7302367763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6x+\\frac{2}{3x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349676} {:answer/id #uuid "056f0598-5b22-5385-8ed6-0a03e4dba74e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6x+\\frac{1}{3x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56f788fc-a267-5197-9a25-a60283bfb398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6x-\\frac{1}{3x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349674} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c82e7b-4e55-535b-a69e-435cf64004e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f6a3026-fcc0-5aa9-8872-9a4b820d514c" :question/math-academy-id "q-334144" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=-6x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}+36xy+108{x}^{2}-6\n$$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." :question/worked-solution "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}+36xy+108{x}^{2}-6,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=3,\\,b(x)=36x,\\,c(x)=108{x}^{2}-6.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=-6x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-6$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z-6x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-6.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-6=3(z-6x)^{2}+36x(z-6x)+108{x}^{2}-6.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-6 & =3(36{x}^{2}-12xz+{z}^{2})+36xz-216{x}^{2}+108{x}^{2}-6 \\\\ {z}^{′}-6 & =3{z}^{2}-6 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =3{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =3x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y+6x$ (that is, $y=z-6x$) to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y+6x & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}-6x \\\\  & =-6x-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
